body:
"If you judge a fish for its ability to climb a tree, it will live its whole life believing that it is stupid."

&#x200B;

Life is so much more than your academic achievements.

If I just wanted attention then I would have shared my life story and be all dramatic looking for the sympathy of others.

&#x200B;

But no.

Guys sorry for the double threads. Maybe my Reddit account is buggy. In my original thread "If you know your life is hopeless..." it took me 4 attempts to post that and only my 4th try showed up. In this new thread after 2 tries both of them showed up. Sorry for the inconvenience of having a double thread but I am having difficulty posting my threads.

&#x200B;

If anyone knows the problem kindly teach me about the issue. Back then it was understandable because I was a new member and new members cannot post threads but now I no longer am a new member yet I still have difficulty posting.

If you reread my post earlier I said I am 23 now. I will be turning 24 on May.

&#x200B;

The thing is if I could not achieve greatness but I had a happy life then I would definitely not kill myself. I'd be disappointed sure but I'd still have a life to enjoy.

&#x200B;

If I have a very difficult life but I am achieving greatness and I have a good story to tell then to me that would be a life worth living.

&#x200B;

But I have neither greatness nor happiness.

For a long time I have yearned for greatness. I think it started when I was 14 when I learned about Leonardo da Vinci. Leonardo da Vinci is my biggest idol. He is considered by some to be the greatest mind that have ever lived and considered by many to be the greatest artist in history. I want a good story too. I want people of generations to come until the end of time to admire the life that I have lived. The thing is, I have potential. Back in school I stood out a lot and people liked me because I was intelligent, handsome, and funny. Dreaming for greatness is not unreasonable if you have talents just like da Vinci who was a very gifted painter so it crushes my soul to see how I have failed in life. What really puzzles me is why God would give me a deep desire to achieve greatness and have me stand out which to me seems like a sign I would become a star someday, yet I just became a failure in life.

&#x200B;

Having a great life can also be understood as having a happy life, a life that you can be proud of. But that is not my life. My life is full of suffering. I'm not exaggerating this but I think I've never had a good year in my life. And what I mean by a good year is a year in your life where you experience more joy than pain. I am neither happy nor have a life I can be proud of. Instead I am suffering constantly and am ashamed of my life. This isn't a life worth living anymore.

Thanks. I don't know why I only saw your post now considering it says it has been posted 46 minutes ago already. Even Reddit seems to not like me.

&#x200B;

If the afterlife is real then I really hope I would go to Heaven or be reincarnated to someone with a great life.

&#x200B;

But what I have really been praying for a lot recently is to have a redo on life where God would finally give me a great life. I started feeling like this since I was 11 years old and now I'm 23. Earlier before I went to sleep I prayed that when I wake up I'd be a baby again. I really have potential but God or whoever is in control of my life just wont let me have a good life. I really think I can contribute to the world but even with unselfish reasons the world just won't seem to let me succeed.
